## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates ability to design data-rights enforcement in OTCA with cross-region flows and immutable stores.

## Key Concepts
- Deletion token propagation
- Tombstone and GC semantics for Kafka
- Immutable storage considerations (Parquet/S3)
- Auditability and legal holds
- Schema-versioning to avoid replay risks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: emit tombstone and propagate deletion token
function deleteTenantData(tenantId){
  emitKafkaTombstone(tenantId);
  purgeDerivedFeatures(tenantId);
  markParquetShardsDeleted(tenantId);
  updateCentralRegistry(tenantId);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test deletion under concurrent deletion requests?
- How would you handle multi-tenant data that migrates regions after deletion?

